items: map-getorelse-emits-copied-on-a-string list-literal-into-an-any-param-is-not-coerced
paths: mod:v1/runtime/backend/rust file:tests/e2e/build-rust-refuses-loudly.sh file:tests/BUGS.md
scope: |
  Two things the review of rozum's branches surfaced, neither of them theirs:
  1. `Map[String,String].getOrElse` emits `.get(&k).copied()`, and `String` has no `Copy` (E0277).
     `.cloned()` is the fix. Found while building a probe -- it masked the real defect I was
     hunting, which is its own argument for fixing it.
  2. MINE: a list LITERAL passed to a parameter declared `Any` is not coerced -- `expected Value,
     found Vec<i64>`. My container coercion covers `Vec<Value>` and `HashMap<String,Value>` targets,
     but for a plain `Any` target `needsAnyCoercion` demands a case class or an already-Value, so a
     literal falls through.
next: fix both, probe each against bin/ssc, then suites
